.TH ALX-TUNE 8 "November 2026" "Algothix OS 0.1.0" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
alx-tune \- hardware auto-tuner and resource-limit manager for Algothix OS (ALX) Lite
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B alx-tune
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B alx-tune
detects system RAM, CPU AES-NI flags, GPU driver, and rotational storage devices,
selects an appropriate hardware profile (\fBalx-profile-low\fR or \fBalx-profile-mid\fR),
writes \fI/etc/alx/profile\fR, and idempotently configures zram (zstd, 50% RAM),
earlyoom, a 1 GB fallback swapfile (when >= 10 GB disk space is free), per-user
systemd slice memory limits, and disabled background services.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-profile " name"
Force hardware profile (\fBalx-profile-low\fR or \fBalx-profile-mid\fR).
.TP
.BI \-\-enable " service"
Re-enable a disabled service (e.g. \fBbluetooth\fR, \fBcups\fR, \fBmodem\fR, \fBavahi\fR).
.TP
.BI \-\-disable " service"
Disable and stop a service.
.TP
.B \-\-dry\-run
Display planned changes without modifying files or services.
.TP
.BI \-\-root " dir"
Operate on an alternate root directory.
.TP
.B \-v, \-\-version
Display version information.
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Display usage information.
.SH FILES
.I /etc/alx/profile
.br
.I /etc/alx/hardware.env
.br
.I /etc/default/zramswap
.br
.I /etc/default/earlyoom
.br
.I /etc/systemd/system/user-.slice.d/50-alx-limits.conf
.br
.I /etc/udev/rules.d/60-alx-io-scheduler.rules
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR alx-doctor (1)
